{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our 20 mg/mL supply to a plant classified VAI 548 days after the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D10"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the methylprednisolone acetate injection shortage on 2021-12-15 and it remains current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E27", "D13"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The 20 mg/mL, 5 mL vials used at Corvale East and Corvale General are labeled by Pharmacia & Upjohn Company LLC (FEI 1810189) per NDC 00009027401.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E6", "E18"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspected that plant on 2023-06-16 and classified it VAI, which was 548 days after the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "An earlier VAI classification letter for the same plant is dated 2018-11-13, 1128 days before the posting, and the most recent letter is dated 2024-09-10, 1000 days after the posting.",
      "cites": ["D11", "D12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Additional current shortage entries list Amneal Pharmaceuticals, Eugia US LLC, Par Health USA LLC, Pfizer Inc., and Sagent Pharmaceuticals as affected manufacturers.",
      "cites": ["E22", "E23", "E24", "E25", "E26"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 2.7 days of the 20 mg/mL vials on hand while Corvale General has 22.8 days.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The top-ranked action is to transfer 61 vials of 20 mg/mL, 5 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would leave the sender with 14 days and bring the receiver to 13 days.",
      "cites": ["D14"]
    }
  ]
}
